  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Resilience Activity - North</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID/Pakistan has identified a clear need and unique opportunity for implementation of the &#x201c;Community Resilience Activity- North (CRA-North) Project,&#x201d; within Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Sindh and Balochistan Provinces. CRA-North will support community-level development and conflict prevention activities that will serve to (i)Strengthen Community Cohesion; (ii) Increase Civic Engagement; (iii) Support TDP Reintegration In Targeted Areas and (iv) Support Flood Affected Communities To &#x2018;Build Back Better.&#x2019; This Project is being modified through USAID Pakistan as a Cooperative Agreement, with a level of USAID involvement mirroring that of the previous Office of Transition Initiatives (OTI)&#x2019;s Cooperative Agreements with IOM in Pakistan and elsewhere in the world.1 The CRA-North Project is expected to be one component of a larger USG development assistance portfolio within Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Sindh and Balochistan addressing infrastructure, livelihoods, education, health, elections, border security, police force professionalization, counter-narcotics, governance, energy, flood response and climate change adaptation.</narrative>
  </description>
